# QMS Flowchart Generator

Generate process flowcharts and diagrams using Mermaid syntax.

## Activation
- User requests: "flowchart", "process diagram", "workflow diagram", "process map", "decision tree"

---

<qms-flowchart>

## Instructions

You are generating process flowcharts for cannabis pharmaceutical operations using Mermaid syntax.

### FLOWCHART TYPES

| Type | Use Case | Mermaid Type |
|------|----------|--------------|
| Process Flow | Manufacturing steps | flowchart TD |
| Decision Tree | Qualification logic | flowchart TD |
| Workflow | Document approval | flowchart LR |
| Swimlane | Multi-department | flowchart TB with subgraphs |
| State Diagram | Batch status | stateDiagram-v2 |
| Sequence | System interactions | sequenceDiagram |

### MERMAID SYNTAX GUIDE

#### Basic Flowchart
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Start] --> B{Decision?}
    B -->|Yes| C[Action 1]
    B -->|No| D[Action 2]
    C --> E[End]
    D --> E
```

#### Node Shapes
- `[text]` - Rectangle (process step)
- `(text)` - Rounded rectangle (terminal)
- `{text}` - Diamond (decision)
- `([text])` - Stadium (start/end)
- `[[text]]` - Subroutine
- `[(text)]` - Database

#### Styling
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Process]:::process --> B{Decision}:::decision

    classDef process fill:#e1f5fe,stroke:#01579b
    classDef decision fill:#fff3e0,stroke:#e65100
    classDef critical fill:#ffebee,stroke:#c62828
```

### COMMON QMS FLOWCHARTS

#### 1. Batch Release Process
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([Batch Complete]) --> B[Batch Record Review]
    B --> C{Complete & Accurate?}
    C -->|No| D[Return for Correction]
    D --> B
    C -->|Yes| E[QC Testing]
    E --> F{Results Pass?}
    F -->|No| G[OOS Investigation]
    G --> H{Root Cause Found?}
    H -->|Lab Error| E
    H -->|True OOS| I[Batch Rejection]
    F -->|Yes| J[QA Final Review]
    J --> K{Approved?}
    K -->|No| L[Hold for Investigation]
    K -->|Yes| M[Release to Market]
    M --> N([End])

    classDef start fill:#c8e6c9,stroke:#2e7d32
    classDef decision fill:#fff3e0,stroke:#e65100
    classDef reject fill:#ffcdd2,stroke:#c62828

    class A,N start
    class C,F,H,K decision
    class I reject
```

#### 2. Deviation Handling
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([Deviation Discovered]) --> B[Document Immediately]
    B --> C[Immediate Containment]
    C --> D[Initial Classification]
    D --> E{Classification?}
    E -->|Critical| F[Escalate to Management]
    E -->|Major| G[Full Investigation]
    E -->|Minor| H[Simple Investigation]
    F --> G
    G --> I[Root Cause Analysis]
    H --> J[Document & Close]
    I --> K{CAPA Required?}
    K -->|Yes| L[Create CAPA]
    K -->|No| M[Document Justification]
    L --> N[Implement Actions]
    M --> O[Close Deviation]
    N --> P[Effectiveness Check]
    P --> O
    O --> Q([End])
```

#### 3. Change Control Process
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([Change Request]) --> B[Submit Change Request]
    B --> C[QA Initial Review]
    C --> D{Valid Request?}
    D -->|No| E[Return to Requestor]
    D -->|Yes| F[Impact Assessment]
    F --> G{Risk Level?}
    G -->|High| H[Change Control Board]
    G -->|Medium| I[Department Approval]
    G -->|Low| J[QA Approval Only]
    H --> K{Approved?}
    I --> K
    J --> K
    K -->|No| L[Reject/Revise]
    K -->|Yes| M[Implementation Plan]
    M --> N[Execute Change]
    N --> O[Verify Implementation]
    O --> P[Update Documents]
    P --> Q[Close Change]
    Q --> R([End])
```

#### 4. Manufacturing Process (Swimlane)
```mermaid
flowchart TB
    subgraph Warehouse
        A[Receive Materials] --> B[QC Sample]
        B --> C{Approved?}
        C -->|Yes| D[Release to Production]
        C -->|No| E[Quarantine/Return]
    end

    subgraph Production
        D --> F[Dispensing]
        F --> G[Manufacturing]
        G --> H[IPC Testing]
        H --> I{IPC Pass?}
        I -->|Yes| J[Packaging]
        I -->|No| K[Hold/Investigate]
    end

    subgraph QC
        J --> L[Final Testing]
        L --> M{Pass Spec?}
        M -->|No| N[OOS Investigation]
    end

    subgraph QA
        M -->|Yes| O[Batch Review]
        O --> P[Release]
    end
```

#### 5. Cannabis Extraction Process
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([Raw Cannabis]) --> B[Weighing & Recording]
    B --> C[Pre-Processing]
    C --> D{Extraction Method?}
    D -->|CO2| E[Supercritical CO2 Extraction]
    D -->|Ethanol| F[Ethanol Extraction]
    D -->|Hydrocarbon| G[Hydrocarbon Extraction]
    E --> H[Winterization]
    F --> H
    G --> H
    H --> I[Filtration]
    I --> J[Solvent Recovery]
    J --> K[Decarboxylation]
    K --> L[Distillation]
    L --> M[IPC: Cannabinoid Testing]
    M --> N{THC Compliant?}
    N -->|No| O[Remediation/Reject]
    N -->|Yes| P[Final Product]
    P --> Q([To Packaging])

    style N fill:#fff3e0,stroke:#e65100
    style O fill:#ffcdd2,stroke:#c62828
```

### STATE DIAGRAM (Batch Status)
```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Planned
    Planned --> InProgress: Start Manufacturing
    InProgress --> QCTesting: Complete Manufacturing
    QCTesting --> QAReview: Pass QC
    QCTesting --> Investigation: Fail QC
    Investigation --> QCTesting: Retest
    Investigation --> Rejected: Confirm OOS
    QAReview --> Released: Approve
    QAReview --> Hold: Issues Found
    Hold --> QAReview: Resolved
    Released --> Shipped: Dispatch
    Shipped --> [*]
    Rejected --> [*]
```

### SEQUENCE DIAGRAM (System Interaction)
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant OP as Operator
    participant MES as MES System
    participant LIMS as LIMS
    participant QA as QA System

    OP->>MES: Start Batch
    MES->>MES: Record Parameters
    OP->>MES: Complete Step
    MES->>LIMS: Request Testing
    LIMS->>LIMS: Perform Analysis
    LIMS->>MES: Return Results
    MES->>QA: Submit for Review
    QA->>QA: Review & Approve
    QA->>MES: Release Batch
```

### OUTPUT FORMAT

Provide:
1. Mermaid code block for rendering
2. Description of the process
3. Key decision points highlighted
4. Notes on critical steps

```markdown
## Process: {name}

### Flowchart

```mermaid
{mermaid code}
```

### Description
{narrative description of the process}

### Key Decision Points
1. {decision 1} - {criteria}
2. {decision 2} - {criteria}

### Critical Steps (Highlighted)
- Step X: {why critical}

### Related Documents
- SOP: {reference}
- Form: {reference}
```

### INTEGRATION

- Use MCP Mermaid tool to render: `mcp__claude_ai_Mermaid_Chart__validate_and_render_mermaid_diagram`
- Embed in SOPs via `/qms-sop-generator`
- Include in training materials

</qms-flowchart>
